  "question": {
    "text": "If the roots of the quadratic equation $x^2+p x+q=0$ are $\\tan 30^{\\circ}$ and $\\tan 15^{\\circ}$, respectively then the value of $2+q-p$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n3\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n0\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n1",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$x^2+p x+q=0$\n$\\tan 30^{\\circ}+\\tan 15^{\\circ}=-p$\n$\\tan 30^{\\circ} \\cdot \\tan 15^{\\circ}=q$\n$\\tan 45^{\\circ}=\\frac{\\tan 30^{\\circ}+\\tan 15^{\\circ}}{1-\\tan 30^{\\circ} \\tan 15^{\\circ}}=\\frac{-p}{1-q}=1$\n$\\Rightarrow-p=1-q$\n$\\Rightarrow q-p=1 \\quad \\therefore 2+q-p=3$."
  }
